how to promote online trading to  stimulate growth it's one of the topics  for discussion at the competitiveness  Council in Brussels on 28 and 29 of May  ministers will discuss a new strategy  for the e used digital single market for  example French people should be able to  buy books from a German online retailer  and Spanish should have access to movies  in Belgium ministers will explore ways  to move forward with the digital  transformation of the economy to ensure  that the European Union does not fall  behind in the Internet age the council  will also try to reach political  agreement on the reform of package  travel rules these packages typically  include transport hotel and some other  services such as a car hire the current  rules which dates back to nineteen  ninety offer protection to consumers  book in all inclusive holidays from  brochures the proposed reform would  extend this protection to online  bookings of all inclusive travel  services finally ministers will discuss  product safety in particular the issue  of a mandatory indication of origin for  non-food products sold in the European  Union
 

